## void vc\_putMemoryValueF(vc\_handle, U indx, char, char *)  
This routine works similar to the vc\_putValueF routine except that it is for passing values to a memory element instead of to a reg or bit. You enter an argument to specify the element (index) to which you want the routine to pass the value. For example:  
```
#include <stdio.h> #include "DirectC.h" void assigner (vc_handle h1, vc_handle h2, vc_handle h3, vc_handle h4) { vc_putMemoryValueF(h1, 0, "10", 'b'); vc_putMemoryValueF(h2, 0, "11", 'o'); vc_putMemoryValueF(h3, 0, "10", 'd'); vc_putMemoryValueF(h4, 0, "aff", 'x'); }
